            <ArticleTitle>Boosting anticancer vaccines: Too much of a good thing?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e25032</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Using both transplantable and oncogene-driven autochthonous tumor models challenged with dendritic cell-based vaccines, we have recently found that boosting provides a clear advantage in prophylactic settings, unless performed on an excessively tight schedule, which causes the loss of central memory T cells. In therapeutic settings, boosting turned out to be always detrimental.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
